From 06e1294ded4cb99a9ba8171e941fc4d5e4cc42c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosetta <its-rosetta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:34:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(appearance): support per-person palette overrides behind
 the shared default

The Settings appearance write stays the shared default for everybody and
the Settings UI is untouched. A provider-established or claimed principal
can store a personal override on a downstream-namespaced row in the
existing app_theme table (no schema change) through the additive
/settings/p6r-personal-appearance PUT/DELETE routes; /system/config then
resolves that principal's palette as override-else-shared and carries an
optional p6rPaletteRoster of each recently seen person's choice for a
future override UI or plugin. The local operator and unclaimed requests
have no personal row, so single-user installs and the CLI are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
